Aim

To create a cloud organization in Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) and manage users and resources.

Requirements
Laptop/Desktop
Internet connection
Oracle Cloud account
Step 1: Open Oracle Cloud Website

Open browser and go to:

Oracle Cloud Free Tier

Click:

Start for free

Step 2: Create Oracle Cloud Account

Fill the details:

Name
Email
Password
Country = India

Verify:

Email OTP
Mobile OTP

Add:

Debit/Credit card for verification
(Oracle usually charges ₹1 temporarily and refunds it)

After verification:

Your Oracle Cloud account will be created.
Step 3: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console Login

Enter:

Cloud Account Name
Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 4: Open OCI Console

After login you will see:

Dashboard
Navigation Menu
Cloud Services

Click:

Top Left Menu (☰)

Step 5: Create a Compartment

Compartment means a folder for cloud resources.

Steps:

Click:

Identity & Security

Click:

Compartments

Click:

Create Compartment

Fill:

Name = MyLabCompartment
Description = Cloud Lab Resources

Click:

Create Compartment

Now compartment is created successfully.

Step 6: Create a User

Steps:

Go to:

Identity & Security

Click:

Users

Click:

Create User

Enter:

Name = student1
Description = Lab User

Click:

Create

Step 7: Create a Group

Steps:

Go to:

Identity & Security

Click:

Groups

Click:

Create Group

Enter:

Name = Developers
Description = Developer Group

Click:

Create

Step 8: Add User to Group

Steps:

Open the group Developers

Click:

Add User to Group

Select:

student1

Click:

Add

User is added successfully.

Step 9: Create Policy

Policy gives permission.

Steps:

Go to:

Identity & Security

Click:

Policies

Click:

Create Policy

Enter:

Name = LabPolicy

In policy statement type:

Allow group Developers to manage all-resources in compartment MyLabCompartment

Click:

Create

Step 10: Create Virtual Cloud Network (VCN)

Steps:

Click:

Networking

Click:

Virtual Cloud Networks

Click:

Start VCN Wizard

Select:

VCN with Internet Connectivity

Click:

Start VCN Wizard

Enter:

VCN Name = MyVCN
Compartment = MyLabCompartment

Click:

Next
Then:
Create

VCN will be created.

Step 11: Create Compute Instance

Steps:

Go to:

Compute

Click:

Instances

Click:

Create Instance

Enter:

Name = MyServer

Select:

Image = Oracle Linux
Shape = Always Free Eligible

Click:

Create

Wait 2–5 minutes.

Instance will start running.

Step 12: Verify Resources

Check:

Compartment created
User created
Group created
Policy working
VCN available
Compute instance running
Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Created Oracle Cloud Organization
Created compartment
Created users and groups
Configured policies
Created VCN
Launched compute instance

Oracle Cloud environment was configured successfully.
